          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"summary\">Summary</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Key concepts:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Functional dependencies</strong> determine normalization steps</li>\n<li><strong>1NF</strong>: Atomic values, no repeating groups</li>\n<li><strong>2NF</strong>: Remove partial dependencies (for composite keys)</li>\n<li><strong>3NF</strong>: Remove transitive dependencies</li>\n<li><strong>BCNF</strong>: Every determinant is a superkey</li>\n<li><strong>Views</strong> can provide denormalized access without storing redundant data</li>\n<li>Always normalize first, then selectively denormalize for performance</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Next week</strong>: Performance and Indexing</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
